### StudyFlow AI — Phase 1 manual verification collection
### REST Client (VS Code) / IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax. Every endpoint built in Phase 1
### (specs/00 through specs/10) is exercised here in the order a real user would hit them.
### Run against a local dev server: cd backend && ./run-dev.sh

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@email = demo@example.com
@password = correct horse battery

### 1. Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Demo Student",
  "birthYear": 2000
}

### 2. Login — copy the accessToken from the response into @accessToken below,
### and copy the refresh_token cookie value into @refreshCookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Current user
@accessToken = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@refreshCookie = PASTE_REFRESH_COOKIE_VALUE_HERE
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Upload a document (multipart) — set Idempotency-Key to a fresh UUID per real attempt
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=studyflow-boundary

--studyflow-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# Sample notes
This is a small test document for the upload endpoint.
--studyflow-boundary--

### 5. Poll the ingest job — copy jobId from the upload response
@jobId = PASTE_JOB_ID_HERE
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6. List documents (cursor-paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. Get one document — copy documentId from the upload response
@documentId = PASTE_DOCUMENT_ID_HERE
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 8. Upload a second, separate document for the not-ready check below — copy its
### documentId into @notReadyDocumentId. Don't reuse @documentId: by the time the
### error-path checks run it has already reached READY (and later gets soft-deleted).
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=studyflow-boundary

--studyflow-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes-not-ready.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# Sample notes for the not-ready check
This document is used to catch the 409 DOCUMENT_NOT_READY window.
--studyflow-boundary--

### 9. Summary requested before ingestion finishes -> 409 DOCUMENT_NOT_READY. Run this
### immediately after step 8, before polling/waiting for that document to reach READY.
@notReadyDocumentId = PASTE_NOT_READY_DOCUMENT_ID_HERE
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{notReadyDocumentId}}/summaries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### 10. Request a summary (only once the document from step 4/7 is READY)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}/summaries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### 11. Poll the summary job — copy jobId from step 10's response
@summaryJobId = PASTE_SUMMARY_JOB_ID_HERE
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{summaryJobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12. List summaries for the document
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}/summaries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 13. Refresh (cookie-authenticated — most HTTP clients replay cookies automatically
### after step 2; if not, the explicit Cookie header below using @refreshCookie makes this
### runnable standalone. X-Request-Id is required — see docs/DECISIONS.md's interim CSRF
### mitigation for /auth/refresh and /auth/logout.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
X-Request-Id: manual-verification-refresh
Cookie: refresh_token={{refreshCookie}}

### 14. Logout — revokes the whole refresh-token family
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
X-Request-Id: manual-verification-logout
Cookie: refresh_token={{refreshCookie}}

### 15. Delete a document (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- Error-path checks worth re-running by hand ---

### 16. Duplicate registration -> 409 AUTH_EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Demo Student",
  "birthYear": 2000
}

### 17. Wrong password -> 401 AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS (same code/message as unknown email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "not the right password"
}

### 18. Unmapped route -> 404 NOT_FOUND (RFC 9457 problem+json)
GET {{baseUrl}}/this-route-does-not-exist
